2:T6f4,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does kitchen fitting labour cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, straightforward kitchen fitting labour may cost around £2,000 to £5,000, but complex layouts, additional trades and specialist materials can raise the price. Every project is different, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does a kitchen fitter’s day rate include?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A day rate normally covers the fitter’s labour for agreed installation work. It may not include materials, waste disposal, plumbing, electrical work, tiling, decorating or specialist worktop installation, so check the quotation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is kitchen fitting labour cheaper if I buy the kitchen myself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be, but only if the design, quantities and components are correct. You may also need to arrange delivery, deal with missing parts and pay for return visits if the kitchen is not ready to install."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to fit a kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A straightforward kitchen may take several working days. A full renovation involving rewiring, plumbing changes, flooring, tiling or structural alterations can take substantially longer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should a kitchen fitting quote include plumbing and electrical work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It should clearly state whether those tasks are included, excluded or priced separately. Ask for them to be listed individually so you can compare quotations on the same basis."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitting-labour-cost-uk","d"]
